# What goes into the sdist beyond the module itself.
#
# The tarball is for someone building or packaging the library, not for someone
# reading about it -- the prose and the generated reference live in the repo and
# on Pages, where they can be read without downloading anything.  So the rule
# here is: ship what a build or a `pytest` run needs, and nothing else.
#
# setuptools picks up tests/test_*.py on its own but not conftest.py, which is
# where every fixture lives -- an sdist with one and not the other ships a test
# suite that cannot collect.  Downstream packagers build from the sdist and run
# the suite to decide whether the build is good, so it is included in full.
recursive-include tests *.py

# The licence is a legal requirement in the distribution, and README.md is what
# `readme = "README.md"` in pyproject.toml renders into the PyPI description --
# leave that one out and the build fails.
include LICENSE
include README.md

# Never ship the caches, the built page, or the editor and agent configuration.
# The prunes are belt-and-braces: setuptools does not reach into these on its
# own, but a stray `include` upstream of here should not be able to leak them.
global-exclude *.py[cod]
global-exclude .DS_Store
prune site
prune __pycache__
prune .claude
prune .vscode
prune pdfs
